  "narration": {
    "title": "The Week Sorts the Hot From the Cold",
    "intro": "Some bats caught fire this week; a few good ones went quiet. On the mound, only one arm is trending up while the rest hold or slip. Here's who moved.",
    "risers_lead": "Michael Massey had the loudest week of anyone, 12-for-21 with two homers for a 1.514 OPS, just ahead of Pittsburgh's Rafael Flores Jr. (8-for-18, three homers). Alejandro Kirk quietly drove in eight over six games in Toronto.",
    "pfallers_lead": "Nick Martinez took the biggest step back among strong arms, down five points to a 69 form score, with Drew Rasmussen slipping four to 77. Neither is in trouble, just cooling.",
    "hweek_lead": "Same names, same heat: Massey and Flores Jr. topped 1.500 for the week, and Vinnie Pasquantino joined the Royals party at 7-for-15.",
    "fallers_lead": "Elly De La Cruz had a rough week at 4-for-29, and Kyle Schwarber went just 3-for-22, though a .027 dip on the season barely dents either resume. Mike Trout's 3-for-22 was the quietest of the group.",
    "colors_lead": "No tier changes to report this week. The board held steady, which after a busy stretch counts as its own kind of news."
  }
